<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31581" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏb-audĭo</span></b> , ii,
		4, v. a., for oboedio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to obey</i> (post-class.); constr. with
				dat. or <i>absol.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 136, 11</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adam non obaudiit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 2, 2</span></i>
			.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obaudite me,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eccles. 39, 17</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏbaudĭens</span></b> , entis,
				<i>P. a., obedient</i> (eccl. Lat. for
			oboediens).— <i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid obaudientius esse potest, quam ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
